  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "uk-gdpr-art-5",
      "title": "UK GDPR Article 5",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/eur/2016/679/article/5",
      "opened": "2026-11-16",
      "taken": "Article 5(1)(d): personal data shall be accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date; every reasonable step must be taken to ensure that personal data that are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed, are erased or rectified without delay (accuracy). Article 6 and Article 9 were not opened. Article 84B was not opened. No lawful basis is asserted. accuracy_met stays false. This starter does not erase or rectify a contact."
    },
    {
      "id": "accessibility-regs",
      "title": "The Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility Regulations 2018",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2018/952",
      "opened": "2026-11-16",
      "taken": "SI 2018/952. The contents page and regulations 3, 4, 6, and 8 were opened. Regulation 3 defines the accessibility requirement as making a website or mobile application perceivable, operable, understandable and robust. Regulation 4(2)(g) says the Regulations do not apply to content of extranets and intranets published before 23rd September 2019, until such websites undergo a substantial revision. Regulation 4(3)(b) defines extranets and intranets as a website that is only available for a closed group of people and not to the general public. Regulation 6: subject to regulation 7, public sector bodies must comply with the accessibility requirement. Regulation 7 was not opened. Regulation 8(1): a public sector body must provide an accessibility statement and keep that statement under regular review. The pages said there are currently no known outstanding effects for regulations 4, 6, and 8. This starter does not decide whether a page is in scope and does not assess that requirement."
    },
    {
      "id": "service-standard",
      "title": "Service Standard",
      "url": "https://www.gov.uk/service-manual/service-standard",
      "opened": "2026-11-16",
      "taken": "The index lists 14 points. Point 5, opened the same day, is Make sure everyone can use the service: provide a service that everyone can use, including disabled people and people with other legally protected characteristics. Point 8, opened the same day, is Iterate and improve frequently: make sure you have the capacity, resources and technical flexibility to iterate and improve the service frequently. The point 8 page says services are never finished. Point 5 was last updated 30 May 2022, with no change to the point itself. This is the Service Standard. It is not a finding that an intranet met it."
    },
    {
      "id": "content-design",
      "title": "Understand content design",
      "url": "https://www.gov.uk/guidance/content-design/what-is-content-design",
      "opened": "2026-11-16",
      "taken": "The page is GOV.UK content and publishing guidance. It says well designed GOV.UK content should be kept up to date, and that content should either be current, meeting a user need and kept up to date, or no longer current but kept as a record of the government's past work. An intranet is not GOV.UK. This starter does not unpublish a page."
    },
    {
      "id": "graph-sitepage",
      "title": "sitePage resource type",
      "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/sitepage?view=graph-rest-1.0",
      "opened": "2026-11-16",
      "taken": "Microsoft Graph v1.0. A sitePage is a page in the sitePages list. Properties opened that day include title, name, description, contentType, createdDateTime, lastModifiedDateTime, pageLayout, publishingState, promotionKind, and webUrl. The property list does not include a content owner, a review interval, a last-reviewed date, or page views. Those are starter fields on the synthetic inventory. This starter does not call Graph. The list-pages permission table was not re-opened on this date."
    },
    {
      "id": "graph-planner-task",
      "title": "plannerTask resource type",
      "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/plannertask?view=graph-rest-1.0",
      "opened": "2026-11-16",
      "taken": "Microsoft Graph v1.0. A plannerTask belongs to a plan and can be assigned to a bucket. The create-task page, opened the same day, is POST /planner/tasks. Delegated least privileged permission shown is Tasks.ReadWrite. Application least privileged permission shown is Tasks.ReadWrite.All. planId must be an existing plan. This starter does not call the API. A task stub in the JSON is not a Planner task."
    },
    {
      "id": "power-automate-approvals",
      "title": "Get started with Power Automate approvals",
      "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-automate/get-started-approvals",
      "opened": "2026-11-16",
      "taken": "The page says that when you submit an approval, approvers are notified. Start and wait for an approval waits for the response. Approve/Reject - First to respond completes when any assigned approver approves or rejects. Approval flows are saved in Dataverse. The approvals connector is described as a standard connector. This starter does not call the connector and does not send the approval request. The only message a deployment of that action would send, in this design, is that approval request to the named content owner."
    },
    {
      "id": "harnesses",
      "title": "Harnesses in Copilot Studio",
      "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/harnesses-overview",
      "opened": "2026-11-16",
      "taken": "The page names three harnesses: Microsoft Copilot harness, Customer Conversation harness, and standard harness. The standard harness powers rule-based agents. The comparison table says it follows the topics and rules you define. The Microsoft Copilot harness is described for reasoning-heavy multi-step work. It supports skills and memory, creates and edits files, and runs each task in a secure sandbox. Agents on this harness use Copilot Credits. The page states no price. The page opened on this date does not use the words GitHub Copilot harness and does not say it is not the GitHub Copilot service. That older wording is unverified against this page."
    }
  ],
